      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Name resolution maps every identifier use to a declaration, and inner declarations shadow outer ones.",
      "narration": "Name resolution links each identifier use to its declaration. Scopes nest, so an inner declaration shadows the outer one until its scope ends.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Shadowing",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "int x = 1;\n{\n  int x = 2;   // shadows\n  print(x);    // 2\n}\nprint(x);      // 1",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 18,
          "w": 84,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "at": 1300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9500,
      "caption": "The compiler keeps a stack of scopes; each scope is a map from names to symbols.",
      "narration": "Implement it as a stack of hash maps from names to symbols. Entering a block pushes a map, and leaving pops it.",
